Used in Vector LCD (profiles/dmg-01-stn.json, dmg-stn.js):
 - the Nintendo DMG-01 five-state palette (from BGB's "The reality of DMG colors")
 - the generated STN director-drift, target and optical tables
   (shaders/dmg01-stn-surrogate.inc, from generated/ws2-stn-physics-v1.json)
 - the contrast-wheel conditions, temperature activation, ionic retention
   defaults and sticking-voltage fit (shaders/dmg01-response-v1.slang)
 - the reflector-shadow strength and offset (shaders/dmg01-display-v1.slang)
 - panel geometry and drive record (data/dmg-drive-v1.json)
Source commit b75171026b1f0594a8288232ad532285470dbe08 (2026-08-25).

Changes: the values were copied into one JSON profile by
tools/dmg01_profile.mjs; no value was changed. The integration follows
Retro Display Lab's dmg01-response-v1.slang (per-frame drift, contrast
interpolation, canonical projection on a drive change, ionic charge and
release, Simpson exposure), re-implemented in WebGL2. The pixel aperture,
passive-matrix crosstalk and row-latch scan-out are not used, because this
panel has no dot grid. The reflector shadow is applied wherever the shifted
image is darker than the point, instead of only in the inter-pixel gaps.
